    "body": "### Motivation\n- SOS navigation refused non-numeric alert identifiers and skipped backend assist lookup, breaking links that use non-numeric/local IDs and allowing special characters to produce malformed requests.\n\n### Description\n- Treat any non-empty `alertId` as valid for backend lookup instead of requiring digits only by normalizing `alertId` with `String(alertId || \"\").trim()` in `SOSNavigate.jsx`.\n- URL-encode the `alertId` when calling the assist endpoint by using `encodeURIComponent(normalizedAlertId)` in the request to `/api/emergency/:alertId/assist`.\n\n### Testing\n- Ran `npm run build` which completed successfully.\n- Ran `npm run lint` which failed due to many pre-existing lint issues elsewhere in the repository and not introduced by this change.\n\n------\n[Codex Task](https://chatgpt.com/codex/tasks/task_b_69b505fbc9c48330a340c59a153bcfde)",
